EXTERNAL flag(name)
Before dawn, the horn.
You've never heard it before, and you know it at once. Everyone does. It goes on longer than any breath should last, and when it stops the whole sky is listening.
The doors of the hall open. The einherjar come out in rows, all the dead you've stamped through, and some of them wave to you as they pass. You recognise a few. You'd hoped you would.
Skögul rides past on a grey horse. She doesn't stop. She lifts her spear to you once, and then she's gone with the rest.
The clerk is at his table, very pale, with his quill in his hand. The ravens sit together at the end of yours for the first time, not arguing.
"Well," says the clerk. "I suppose we'd better start." # speaker: clerk
{ flag("clerk_contract"):
  He touches the drawer where your contract is, as if to make sure it's still there.
}
* [Ink the stamps.]
  You ink them one by one. VALHALLA. HEL. FÓLKVANGR. RETURN. RÁN. TRANSFER. DETAIN. Your hands are perfectly steady, which surprises you.
* [Look north.]
  To the north, where the ship was being built, the sky is the colour of a bruise, and something very large is moving on the sea.
- The dead are already coming up the path, all of them at once, and the sun is already sinking.
-> END
